  "comment": "vibe-land's material catalog: one id per surface the city can show, shared by every renderer. The index of an entry with a `layer` is that layer of the web's texture arrays (client/public/textures/city, client/src/scene/cityTextureSets.generated.ts; walls first, then floors, ground, authored) and must stay in that order. Renderers map ids to their own materials: the web samples the array layer; Unreal maps each id to a PBR material (unreal/VibeCity, VibeLandCity). `textureKeys` and `names` are the manifest's material appearance fields (scene packs: materials[].textureKey / name) that resolve to the entry; a material whose textureKey names no entry takes entry 0, as the web does. `polyHaven` is the CC0 source set where there is one (a renderer may load it at higher resolution than the web's 1k sheets); the authored sets are procedural (client/scripts/bake-authored-city.py).",
